# Copy to .env for local dev. Not committed with real values — mock mode is opt-in on purpose so
# a production/TestFlight build never silently serves fake data.

# Base URL of exceed-box-app (FastAPI). REQUIRED for any non-mock build — there is no
# 127.0.0.1/localhost fallback (on a real device that would mean the phone calling itself).
# If this is unset and EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS is not 1, the app shows a configuration-error
# screen instead of guessing an address.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8912

# Real sign-in (src/auth/supabase.ts). REQUIRED for any non-mock build — without both of these,
# both sign-in buttons show a "not configured" error naming exactly what's missing instead of a
# bare throw. No Supabase project exists yet (FABLE-AUDIT.md C2); these are placeholders until
# one is provisioned. The anon key is meant to be public/embeddable (Supabase's own design —
# it's rate-limited and RLS-gated on the server, not a secret), so a plain env var is fine here.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# Set to 1 to serve every SPEC.md endpoint from src/api/mocks.ts instead of the network.
# Sign in with admin@exceed-re.ae / marketing@exceed-re.ae / manager@exceed-re.ae /
# sales@exceed-re.ae (any password) to demo each of the four roles, or "Continue with Google"
# to sign in as the admin demo account.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS=1

# Dev-only, mock mode only: force every list to render empty, to check the empty state.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_EMPTY=1

# Dev-only, mock mode only: force every call to fail, to check the error+retry state.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_ERROR=1
